o make an enemy's head explode  after impact after spending hours slowly  creeping through the shadows and  carefully managing limited ammo  replaying 0 with Wesker's powers is a  cathartic release that almost entirely  changes the tone and pace of the game  it's one of the best examples of replay  value in recent memory  [Music]  despite releasing mere months after Vita  lost in 2012 ahead of hundreds of games  to come gravity rush remains one of the  system's most memorable games when it  made the jump to PlayStation 4 earlier  this year the already great game became  even better it's vibrant graphics were  extensively remastered and his controls  were refined to take advantage of  DualShock 4's capabilities in lieu of  ADA's prominent touchscreen Blue Point  games is renowned for its work porting  games like titanfall to xbox 360 and it  does such a great job moving gravity  rush to the big screen that you'd never  know it was a handheld exclusive to  begin with according to rez creator Ted  CI music Gucci his original vision for  the 2001 game included virtual reality  but because be our technology floundered  for years both before and after Reza's  inception he ultimately had to wait 15  years to realize his dream although res  was beloved when it first came out on  Dreamcast and PlayStation 2 the  remastered version for PlayStation 4 and  PlayStation VR will go down as the  definitive version of music Gucci's  masterpiece flying through Reza's  existing stages in VR enhances the way  you absorb its colors and sounds but  area ex a new level designed just for  res infinite went off the rails allowing  you to freely fly through a shimmering  dreamscape as a whole res infinite  offers an incredible mix of sights and  sounds but area ex in particular is a  hypnotic experience unlike anything else  we've played in VR it looks bad for you  nonsense it makes me feel great smarter  more aggressive Tim Schafer has had an  illustrious career as a game designer  first at